@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.1.30
@changelog
  - Codename: Exsqueeze me? Baking powder?
  - New: global per-surface V-Pot / encoder speed + Fine factor (Settings → Device) — tune UF8 and UC1 independently
  - New: tunable 0 dB virtual notch on UF8 V-Pots AND UC1 knobs (EQ gains / trims / fader level) — snaps reliably to 0 dB on approach; settings for notch zone, fine step near 0, and a soft-detent "hold" so an endless encoder can't overshoot
  - New: pan honours the same V-Pot speed / Fine scaling
  - Fix: Learn-HUD "End() too many times" crash (hardware-layout tab / collapsed HUD); geometry-section parse hardened
  - Fix: stale pre-ReaImGui companion scripts removed on load, so an old Action can no longer launch the broken gfx HUD
